hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3074","Narrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir, narrated to us Ibn Fudayl, narrated to us Habib ibn Abi 'Amrah, on the authority of 'Aishah bint Talhah, from 'Aishah, the Mother of the Believers (RA), who said:\n\n\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), is there jihad upon women?'\n\nHe (ﷺ) said: 'Yes, upon them is a jihad in which there is no fighting: Hajj and 'Umrah.'\"\n\nAbu Bakr (a commentator) said regarding the statement of the Prophet (ﷺ), \"Upon them is a jihad in which there is no fighting,\" and his clarification that the jihad obligatory upon them is Hajj and 'Umrah, is an explanation that 'Umrah is obligatory like Hajj. For the apparent meaning of his statement, \"Upon them,\" indicates that it is obligatory, as it is not permissible to say of a person that which is voluntary and not obligatory.\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
